   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Animated Line Chart\n\nA line chart whose path draws on from left to right with a glowing leading dot.\n\nCategory: data-viz. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Showing growth or trend over time: a revenue curve, a user climb, an error rate drop.\n- You want a single continuous reveal motion rather than a per-bar stagger.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The data is categorical rather than time-ordered: use a bar chart.\n- You have only two or three points: use a number counter or a headline stat.\n\nVariables:\n- data (string): Data, default \"12, 19, 8, 15, 22, 18, 28, 25, 32\"\n- stroke_color (color): Line colour, default \"#22c55e\"\n- stroke_width (number, 1-16): Line width, default 4\n- grid_color (color): Grid colour, default \"#27272a\"\n- show_dot (boolean): Leading dot, default true\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Animated Line Chart\n\n  A line chart whose path draws on from left to right with a glowing leading dot.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/animated-line-chart/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"animated-line-chart\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\":\"data\",\"type\":\"string\",\"role\":\"content\",\"label\":\"Data\",\"description\":\"Comma-separated numbers, at least two.\",\"default\":\"12, 19, 8, 15, 22, 18, 28, 25, 32\"},{\"id\":\"stroke_color\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Line colour\",\"description\":\"Colour of the line and dot.\",\"default\":\"#22c55e\"},{\"id\":\"stroke_width\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Line width\",\"description\":\"Width of the line.\",\"default\":4,\"min\":1,\"max\":16,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"px\"},{\"id\":\"grid_color\",\"type\":\"color\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Grid colour\",\"description\":\"Colour of the grid and axes.\",\"default\":\"#27272a\"},{\"id\":\"show_dot\",\"type\":\"boolean\",\"role\":\"style\",\"label\":\"Leading dot\",\"description\":\"Show a dot at the drawing tip.\",\"default\":true},{\"id\":\"speed\",\"type\":\"number\",\"role\":\"motion\",\"label\":\"Speed\",\"description\":\"Playback speed multiplier.\",\"default\":1,\"min\":0.25,\"max\":4,\"step\":0.05,\"unit\":\"x\"}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Animated Line Chart</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        #root { background: #09090b; font-family: Geist, system-ui, sans-serif; }\n        .ac-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        #ac-chart { position: absolute; overflow: visible; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"animated-line-chart\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ac-clip\" class=\"ac-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n<svg id=\"ac-chart\" width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" viewBox=\"0 0 1000 500\" style=\"overflow:visible\"></svg>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            // Frame-based helpers, written from their definitions.\n            var Easing = (function () {\n              function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                    var u = 1 - t;\n                    var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (Math.abs(cx - x) < 1e-6) break;\n                    if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var v = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n              return {\n                bezier: bezier,\n                linear: function (t) { return t; },\n                quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n                cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n                sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n                poly: function (n) { return function (t) { return Math.pow(t, n); }; },\n                ease: bezier(0.42, 0, 1, 1),\n                out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n                inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; }\n              };\n            })();\n            function interpolate(input, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var left = o.extrapolateLeft || \"extend\";\n              var right = o.extrapolateRight || \"extend\";\n              var i = 1;\n              while (i < n - 1 && input > inR[i]) i++;\n              var a = inR[i - 1], b = inR[i];\n              if (input < inR[0] && left === \"clamp\") return outR[0];\n              if (input > inR[n - 1] && right === \"clamp\") return outR[n - 1];\n              var t = b === a ? 0 : (input - a) / (b - a);\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i - 1] + (outR[i] - outR[i - 1]) * t;\n            }\n            // Damped spring from rest to 1. durationInFrames stretches time so the spring has settled by then.\n            function spring(o) {\n              var c = o.config || {};\n              var mass = c.mass != null ? c.mass : 1;\n              var k = c.stiffness != null ? c.stiffness : 100;\n              var damp = c.damping != null ? c.damping : 10;\n              function at(t) {\n                var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / mass);\n                var z = damp / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * mass));\n                if (z < 1) {\n                  var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                  return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + ((z * w0) / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n                }\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              }\n              var t = Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.fps;\n              if (o.durationInFrames) {\n                var settle = 4, step = 1 / o.fps;\n                for (var s = settle; s > 0.05; s -= step) {\n                  if (Math.abs(1 - at(s)) > 0.001) { settle = s + step; break; }\n                  settle = s;\n                }\n                t = (Math.max(0, o.frame) / o.durationInFrames) * settle;\n                if (o.frame >= o.durationInFrames) return 1;\n              }\n              return at(t);\n            }\n            function parseColor(c) {\n              var m;\n              c = String(c).trim();\n              if ((m = /^#([0-9a-f]{3,8})$/i.exec(c))) {\n                var h = m[1];\n                if (h.length <= 4) h = h.split(\"\").map(function (x) { return x + x; }).join(\"\");\n                return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16), h.length === 8 ? parseInt(h.slice(6, 8), 16) / 255 : 1];\n              }\n              if ((m = /^rgba?\\(([^)]+)\\)/i.exec(c))) {\n                var p = m[1].split(\",\").map(Number);\n                return [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.length > 3 ? p[3] : 1];\n              }\n              return [0, 0, 0, 1];\n            }\n            function interpolateColors(t, inR, outR) {\n              var a = parseColor(outR[0]), b = parseColor(outR[1]);\n              var u = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (t - inR[0]) / (inR[1] - inR[0])));\n              return \"rgba(\" + [0, 1, 2].map(function (i) { return Math.round(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u); }).join(\",\") + \",\" + (a[3] + (b[3] - a[3]) * u) + \")\";\n            }\n            // Seeded 0..1 value: the same seed always gives the same number.\n            function random(seed) {\n              var s = String(seed), h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\n                h ^= s.charCodeAt(i);\n                h = Math.imul(h, 16777619);\n              }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 16), 3266489917);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 15)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            // Fit a fixed-size design stage into the frame.\n            function fit(el, w, h, fill) {\n              var s = Math.min(root.clientWidth / w, root.clientHeight / h) * (fill || 1);\n              el.style.position = \"absolute\";\n              el.style.left = \"50%\";\n              el.style.top = \"50%\";\n              el.style.width = w + \"px\";\n              el.style.height = h + \"px\";\n              el.style.transform = \"translate(-50%, -50%) scale(\" + s + \")\";\n              return s;\n            }\n            // Drive draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking always draws the same picture.\n            function clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw, rate) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: totalFrames, duration: totalFrames / 30, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame * (rate || 1)); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function svgEl(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n\n                        // Stop-motion helpers: poses are held for `step` frames.\n            var DEFAULT_STEP = 3;\n            function qf(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step) * step; }\n            function qstep(frame, step) { step = step || DEFAULT_STEP; return Math.floor(frame / step); }\n            function hash01(seed) { return random(seed); }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            function paperJitter(frame, seed, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var amp = o.amp != null ? o.amp : 1.4, rotAmp = o.rotAmp != null ? o.rotAmp : 0.35;\n              var s = qstep(frame, o.step);\n              return { x: hashRange(seed + \":x:\" + s, -amp, amp), y: hashRange(seed + \":y:\" + s, -amp, amp), rot: hashRange(seed + \":r:\" + s, -rotAmp, rotAmp) };\n            }\n            function steppedRamp(frame, from, to, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var f = qf(frame, o.step);\n              if (f <= from) return 0;\n              if (f >= to) return 1;\n              var ease = o.ease || function (t) { return t; };\n              return ease((f - from) / (to - from));\n            }\n\n\n            var raw = str(vars.data, \"12, 19, 8, 15, 22, 18, 28, 25, 32\").split(\",\").map(Number).filter(Number.isFinite);\n            var data = raw.length >= 2 ? raw : [12, 19, 8, 15, 22, 18, 28, 25, 32];\n            var stroke = str(vars.stroke_color, \"#22c55e\"), sw = num(vars.stroke_width, 4, 1, 16), grid = str(vars.grid_color, \"#27272a\");\n            var showDot = bool(vars.show_dot, true), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var svg = document.getElementById(\"ac-chart\");\n            var Wc = 1000, Hc = 500;\n            // Fit the chart into the frame (more fill on a tall frame).\n            fit(svg, Wc, Hc, root.clientHeight > root.clientWidth ? 0.9 : 0.78);\n            var pad = 60, iw = Wc - pad * 2, ih = Hc - pad * 2;\n            var min = Math.min.apply(null, data), max = Math.max.apply(null, data), range = max - min || 1;\n            var pts = data.map(function (v, i) { return { x: pad + (i / (data.length - 1)) * iw, y: pad + ih - ((v - min) / range) * ih }; });\n            var len = 0;\n            for (var i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) len += Math.hypot(pts[i].x - pts[i - 1].x, pts[i].y - pts[i - 1].y);\n            var rows = 4, cols = data.length - 1;\n            for (var r = 0; r <= rows; r++) { var gy = pad + (r / rows) * ih; svgEl(\"line\", { x1: pad, x2: pad + iw, y1: gy, y2: gy, stroke: grid, \"stroke-width\": 1 }, svg); }\n            for (var c = 0; c <= cols; c++) { var gx = pad + (c / cols) * iw; svgEl(\"line\", { x1: gx, x2: gx, y1: pad, y2: pad + ih, stroke: grid, \"stroke-width\": 1 }, svg); }\n            svgEl(\"line\", { x1: pad, x2: pad, y1: pad, y2: pad + ih, stroke: grid, \"stroke-width\": 2 }, svg);\n            svgEl(\"line\", { x1: pad, x2: pad + iw, y1: pad + ih, y2: pad + ih, stroke: grid, \"stroke-width\": 2 }, svg);\n            var d = pts.map(function (p, i) { return (i === 0 ? \"M\" : \"L\") + p.x.toFixed(2) + \",\" + p.y.toFixed(2); }).join(\" \");\n            var path = svgEl(\"path\", { d: d, fill: \"none\", stroke: stroke, \"stroke-width\": sw, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\", \"stroke-linejoin\": \"round\", \"stroke-dasharray\": len, \"stroke-dashoffset\": len }, svg);\n            path.style.filter = \"drop-shadow(0 0 12px \" + stroke + \"55)\";\n            var dot = svgEl(\"circle\", { cx: pts[0].x, cy: pts[0].y, r: sw * 2, fill: stroke }, svg);\n            dot.style.filter = \"drop-shadow(0 0 8px \" + stroke + \")\";\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\") * 30);\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var f = frame * speed;\n              var p = spring({ frame: f, fps: 30, durationInFrames: Math.round(totalFrames * 0.85), config: { damping: 200 } });\n              path.setAttribute(\"stroke-dashoffset\", len * (1 - p));\n              var target = len * p, traveled = 0, dx = pts[0].x, dy = pts[0].y;\n              for (var i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\n                var ax = pts[i].x - pts[i - 1].x, ay = pts[i].y - pts[i - 1].y, seg = Math.hypot(ax, ay);\n                if (traveled + seg >= target) { var t = (target - traveled) / seg; dx = pts[i - 1].x + ax * t; dy = pts[i - 1].y + ay * t; break; }\n                traveled += seg; dx = pts[i].x; dy = pts[i].y;\n              }\n              dot.setAttribute(\"cx\", dx); dot.setAttribute(\"cy\", dy);\n              dot.style.display = showDot && p > 0 && p < 1 ? \"\" : \"none\";\n            }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            clockTween(tl, totalFrames, draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"animated-line-chart\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
